From 3285003cc2b4852199411c59b28f6f1ad076cce6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:25:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): [daveey] hub-session opens skip the owner
 lookup and paint from cache; Inbox sessions prefetch first

Opens of another gateway's session were slow (live [open-timing] 2026-10-27):
Inbox cards for hub sessions painted from REST after a 4.5-6.8 s "owner"
stage, and route resumes of an old hub chat (no owner given) never painted
from the transcript cache even though it held them.

- The owner probe (probeStoredSession) only knew $sessions / cron /
  messaging / project-tree rows; hub sessions live in the hub-replica
  fallback rows, so every open did getSession over SSH. A replica row that
  matches the named owner now answers at once (fallbackSessionRow).
- A resume that names no owner takes it from the session's awake replica
  row, so the cached transcript paints before any await (asleep rows keep
  the read-only path).
- The prefetcher put people's chats before automations within 200 slots per
  gateway; the sessions behind open Inbox cards (self-heal, Kanban) are
  automations and never got a slot. Open Inbox items' sessions now go first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
